From: cl2t <yihong.or@isrc.iscas.ac.cn>
Subject: [PATCH] Run periodic interest cleanup within the test window

Only consumer leaders propose replicated stream message deletions. When
leaders process their local consumer acks before the other consumers'
replicated acks, removal waits for the periodic interest sweep. Its default
two-minute interval exceeds this test's 30-second assertion window.

Use the same four-second test interval and one-second jitter as upstream
TestJetStreamClusterInterestStreamConsumer, restoring the defaults after
cluster shutdown. Keep all ten consumers, 10,000 messages, ack floors and
empty-stream assertions.

Based on the fixture adjustment and ordering explanation in:
https://github.com/nats-io/nats-server/commit/44cc2ac1f19d765ad7884ad59aa923d9918e10c0

Signed-off-by: cl2t <yihong.or@isrc.iscas.ac.cn>
---
--- a/server/norace_test.go
+++ b/server/norace_test.go
@@ -7294,6 +7294,17 @@
 }
 
 func TestNoRaceJetStreamInterestStreamCheckInterestRaceBug(t *testing.T) {
+	// Leaders may process their own consumer's ack before the other consumers'
+	// replicated acks arrive. The periodic interest sweep then proposes deletion.
+	// Exercise that sweep within the 30-second assertion window, as in
+	// TestJetStreamClusterInterestStreamConsumer.
+	checkInterestStateT = 4 * time.Second
+	checkInterestStateJ = 1
+	defer func() {
+		checkInterestStateT = defaultCheckInterestStateT
+		checkInterestStateJ = defaultCheckInterestStateJ
+	}()
+
 	c := createJetStreamClusterExplicit(t, "R3S", 3)
 	defer c.shutdown()
 
